The Moment of My Doom Arrived...  Part 1

1196
00:03:38,577 --> 00:03:40,097
In the game's scenario,

1197
00:03:40,097 --> 00:03:42,897
Maria condemns Catarina right after this.

1198
00:03:42,897 --> 00:03:44,647
<i>What they say is true.</i>

1199
00:03:44,647 --> 00:03:48,487
If this plays out the same way, 
Catarina will be exiled all alone!

1200
00:03:48,487 --> 00:03:51,467
That or she'll be killed 
by the conquerable characters.

1201
00:03:51,467 --> 00:03:53,607
Does she have a toy snake in her pocket?

1202
00:03:53,607 --> 00:03:58,017
If she's exiled, will she be able to 
take her favorite hoe with her?

1203
00:03:59,697 --> 00:04:01,557
Well, Maria Campbell...

1204
00:04:01,557 --> 00:04:05,317
Now is the time to prosecute 
Catarina Claes for her crimes!

1205
00:04:08,117 --> 00:04:09,447
All of this...

1206
00:04:13,777 --> 00:04:15,447
is complete rubbish!

1207
00:04:16,617 --> 00:04:17,627
Huh?

1208
00:04:17,627 --> 00:04:20,487
Please don't besmirch someone 
who means so much to me!

1209
00:04:20,487 --> 00:04:24,077
Wh-What are you talking about? 
We're doing this to help you!

1210
00:04:24,077 --> 00:04:26,937
Th-That's right. We have concrete proof!

1211
00:04:26,937 --> 00:04:29,007
We're all on your side!

1212
00:04:29,147 --> 00:04:30,867
Aren't we, Geordo-sama?

1213
00:04:31,347 --> 00:04:35,637
You call circumstantial evidence 
like this "concrete proof"?

1214
00:04:35,637 --> 00:04:37,057
How Laughable.

1215
00:04:38,827 --> 00:04:45,137
My simple-minded sister isn't even 
capable of such elaborate harassment.

1216
00:04:45,557 --> 00:04:49,857
Did you really see my sister doing all this?

1217
00:04:50,967 --> 00:04:52,577
He's right!

1218
00:04:52,577 --> 00:04:55,777
There's no way Catarina-sama 
would do any of these things!

1219
00:04:55,777 --> 00:04:58,317
She's far too simple-minded!

1220
00:04:58,467 --> 00:05:00,247
Yeah, that's right.

1221
00:05:00,247 --> 00:05:03,677
This idiot could never come up 
with such intricate schemes.

1222
00:05:03,677 --> 00:05:06,657
She's so dumb, all she could do 
would be to fight her head-on!

1223
00:05:07,657 --> 00:05:11,617
They're right! 
Catarina-sama isn't that clever!

1224
00:05:11,627 --> 00:05:12,917
Exactly.

1225
00:05:14,037 --> 00:05:15,627
<i>What's going on?</i>

1226
00:05:15,627 --> 00:05:18,847
<i>I think they're sticking up for me,</i>

1227
00:05:18,847 --> 00:05:20,297
<i>but I kind of feel insulted...</i>

1228
00:05:20,517 --> 00:05:23,607
It's true! Catarina-sama would never do such things!

1229
00:05:23,607 --> 00:05:25,307
This must be some kind of mistake.

1230
00:05:25,307 --> 00:05:26,887
Yeah, that's right!

1231
00:05:26,887 --> 00:05:28,737
It's not possible!

1232
00:05:30,557 --> 00:05:32,297
It's true that I've

1233
00:05:32,297 --> 00:05:35,647
been bullied since I came here, 
just like these papers say.

1234
00:05:36,347 --> 00:05:39,147
But it wasn't Catarina-sama who bullied me.

1235
00:05:39,607 --> 00:05:43,107
Catarina-sama has stood up for me many times.

1236
00:05:44,507 --> 00:05:49,627
I clearly remember who it was 
that really bullied me.

1237
00:05:49,627 --> 00:05:53,707
If it's what you want, I'd be glad 
to name them here and now.

1238
00:06:05,247 --> 00:06:06,377
<i>What was that?</i>

1239
00:06:07,317 --> 00:06:09,657
Catarina-sama, are you all right?

1240
00:06:09,657 --> 00:06:11,627
Oh... Yeah.

1241
00:06:11,627 --> 00:06:14,467
Um, thanks, everyone.

1242
00:06:14,467 --> 00:06:19,127
No, we should apologize 
for not being here sooner to help you.

1243
00:06:19,127 --> 00:06:21,367
Sorry we were late, Sister.

1244
00:06:22,347 --> 00:06:25,537
<i>I can finally relax...</i>

1245
00:06:28,957 --> 00:06:32,577
I never expected those girls 
to do such a thing.

1246
00:06:32,687 --> 00:06:36,667
I knew they had a grudge against my sister,

1247
00:06:36,667 --> 00:06:39,967
but I didn't think they 
were the type to act on it like that.

1248
00:06:40,117 --> 00:06:43,587
Regardless of how she is, 
she is the daughter of a duke.

1249
00:06:43,587 --> 00:06:47,267
Slandering her could put 
them in a precarious position.

1250
00:06:47,267 --> 00:06:52,937
Yes, and this list of "proof" doesn't look 
like something they could have come up with.

1251
00:06:53,147 --> 00:06:56,907
Even if it's fake, it's very
competently put together.

1252
00:06:57,107 --> 00:07:01,237
It's also strange that we were all 
called away on student council business.

1253
00:07:01,327 --> 00:07:05,707
It's as if they waited for a time 
when they knew we wouldn't be there.

1254
00:07:08,827 --> 00:07:11,507
<i>Whew, thank goodness!</i>

1255
00:07:11,507 --> 00:07:13,627
<i>I made it through my judgment event!</i>

1256
00:07:13,627 --> 00:07:15,877
<i>I avoided my doom flags!</i>

1257
00:07:15,877 --> 00:07:25,427
Doom

1258
00:07:15,877 --> 00:07:25,427
Doom

1259
00:07:15,877 --> 00:07:25,427
DOOM
FLAG

1260
00:07:16,187 --> 00:07:19,417
<i>The story in the game continues 
until the current second-years graduate,</i>

1261
00:07:19,417 --> 00:07:21,747
<i>so I still can't let my guard down...</i>

1262
00:07:21,747 --> 00:07:25,427
<i>But still, I made it through my 
greatest crisis with all of their help!</i>

1263
00:07:25,427 --> 00:07:27,637
<i>What a relief!</i>

1264
00:07:30,767 --> 00:07:33,387
Ah, today's lunch was as tasty as ever!

1265
00:07:33,387 --> 00:07:37,347
I don't know how you could eat 
so much after what just happened.

1266
00:07:37,347 --> 00:07:39,427
That's part of what makes her so wonderful!

1267
00:07:39,797 --> 00:07:41,267
Thanks!

1268
00:07:46,437 --> 00:07:47,317
Um...

1269
00:07:48,467 --> 00:07:52,117
I'm sorry. You can all head back without me.

1270
00:07:52,357 --> 00:07:55,707
I need to make a quick stop somewhere first.

1271
00:07:55,857 --> 00:07:58,807
Where? Do you want us to go with you?

1272
00:07:58,807 --> 00:08:00,677
I mean, after that whole mess before...

1273
00:08:00,817 --> 00:08:05,047
No, it's nothing important. 
I'll be fine by myself.

1274
00:08:05,047 --> 00:08:06,857
You can all go on ahead.

1275
00:08:06,857 --> 00:08:09,057
All right. We'll see you later, then.

1276
00:08:09,057 --> 00:08:09,797
Okay.

1277
00:08:12,647 --> 00:08:16,657
<i>Later on, I would deeply regret</i>

1278
00:08:16,657 --> 00:08:20,607
<i>not going with Maria at that moment.</i>

1279
00:08:21,457 --> 00:08:23,867
<i>Our lunch break on that day...</i>

1280
00:08:25,087 --> 00:08:27,557
<i>was the last time any of us saw Maria.</i>

1281
00:08:29,177 --> 00:08:34,207
Two Days Later

1282
00:08:29,177 --> 00:08:34,207
Two Days Later

1283
00:08:38,147 --> 00:08:40,967
<i>Why didn't I go with her?</i>

1284
00:08:42,437 --> 00:08:44,677
Warm yourself up with this.

1285
00:08:44,677 --> 00:08:46,277
You're rather pale.

1286
00:08:46,277 --> 00:08:47,557
President...

1287
00:08:47,907 --> 00:08:49,617
Thank you very much.

1288
00:08:53,217 --> 00:08:56,027
<i>The same gentle flavor as always...</i>

1289
00:08:56,837 --> 00:08:59,057
I'm positive Maria-san is just fine.

1290
00:08:59,617 --> 00:09:01,097
Yes...

1291
00:09:01,397 --> 00:09:02,647
<i>The president...</i>

1292
00:09:03,407 --> 00:09:06,747
<i>He was good friends with Maria, too.</i>

1293
00:09:07,387 --> 00:09:11,067
<i>There's no way he isn't upset right now.</i>

1294
00:09:13,077 --> 00:09:14,307
<i>That's right.</i>

1295
00:09:14,307 --> 00:09:16,567
<i>I'm not the only one 
who's struggling with this.</i>

1296
00:09:16,567 --> 00:09:19,297
<i>I can't just sit around 
being sad and regretting it.</i>

1297
00:09:19,637 --> 00:09:22,947
All right! I'm going to find Maria for sure!

1298
00:09:22,947 --> 00:09:25,267
Just stay safe and wait for me, Maria!

1299
00:09:32,547 --> 00:09:36,937
<i>But we couldn't find 
any trace of Maria at all.</i>

1300
00:09:37,477 --> 00:09:39,767
<i>We couldn't even find any clues.</i>

1301
00:09:42,537 --> 00:09:44,537
<i>It's been three days now...</i>

1302
00:09:46,487 --> 00:09:49,337
Catarina-sama, Geordo-sama is here.

1303
00:09:49,337 --> 00:09:50,867
At this hour?

1304
00:09:51,627 --> 00:09:53,317
Did something happen to Maria?!

1305
00:09:53,317 --> 00:09:57,187
No, I still haven't found out where she is,

1306
00:09:57,187 --> 00:10:00,707
but I got some information 
that I must share with you.

1307
00:10:00,707 --> 00:10:02,587
I'm sorry to come over so late.

1308
00:10:02,697 --> 00:10:04,017
Information?

1309
00:10:04,387 --> 00:10:09,197
First, take a look at the papers 
those girls presented as evidence.

1310
00:10:10,377 --> 00:10:14,167
I looked into it, and I 
learned something very strange.

1311
00:10:14,167 --> 00:10:17,167
It wasn't those girls 
that came up with that list.

1312
00:10:17,167 --> 00:10:19,707
Someone else put it together.

1313
00:10:20,597 --> 00:10:22,527
And what's even stranger is that

1314
00:10:22,527 --> 00:10:28,527
the girls have no recollection 
of who they got them from.

1315
00:10:28,527 --> 00:10:30,617
They don't remember?

1316
00:10:30,717 --> 00:10:35,847
I thought they were lying, at first, 
so I checked into some things.

1317
00:10:35,847 --> 00:10:38,817
But it seems like they truly don't remember.

1318
00:10:38,977 --> 00:10:40,667
What could this mean?

1319
00:10:41,087 --> 00:10:44,337
Do they all have amnesia or something?

1320
00:10:44,467 --> 00:10:46,157
It's not only that.

1321
00:10:46,157 --> 00:10:51,467
They don't even remember why they tried 
to do what they did on that day.

1322
00:10:52,587 --> 00:10:56,347
It's true that they have 
unfavorable opinions of you,

1323
00:10:56,707 --> 00:11:01,477
but they say they never even 
considered attempting anything

1324
00:11:01,477 --> 00:11:03,437
that would publicly damage you like that.

1325
00:11:03,437 --> 00:11:04,947
For some reason,

1326
00:11:04,947 --> 00:11:08,867
I was suddenly overwhelmed 
with the urge to do something horrible

1327
00:11:08,867 --> 00:11:10,947
to that detestable Catarina Claes.

1328
00:11:10,947 --> 00:11:13,307
But when I left the cafeteria afterward,

1329
00:11:13,307 --> 00:11:16,007
that feeling had disappeared completely.

1330
00:11:16,227 --> 00:11:21,107
In fact, we're all at a loss 
as to why we did such a thing.

1331
00:11:21,107 --> 00:11:24,667
We're truly, truly sorry!

1332
00:11:24,817 --> 00:11:26,427
That's so strange.

1333
00:11:26,717 --> 00:11:29,587
It's as if someone was controlling them.

1334
00:11:29,747 --> 00:11:32,297
That may be exactly what happened.

1335
00:11:33,457 --> 00:11:37,087
The way those girls were acting 
at the time seemed very odd.

1336
00:11:37,637 --> 00:11:41,437
But how would someone 
manipulate them like that?

1337
00:11:41,597 --> 00:11:44,347
It's possible if one has dark magic.

1338
00:11:44,577 --> 00:11:46,067
Dark magic?

1339
00:11:46,917 --> 00:11:49,497
Dark magic is the sixth type of magic.

1340
00:11:49,497 --> 00:11:51,827
It's very dangerous, 
so it's forbidden to use,

1341
00:11:51,827 --> 00:11:53,337
and it's been kept hidden.

1342
00:11:53,797 --> 00:11:57,207
Only a few people 
in the entire country know about it.

1343
00:11:57,207 --> 00:11:59,737
A kind of magic 
that dangerous actually exists?

1344
00:12:00,617 --> 00:12:03,527
Dark magic can manipulate people's hearts,

1345
00:12:03,527 --> 00:12:07,087
and those it manipulates 
don't remember it afterward.

1346
00:12:09,067 --> 00:12:11,137
What a horrifying power...

1347
00:12:11,847 --> 00:12:12,767
Yes.

1348
00:12:12,767 --> 00:12:15,497
It amplifies emotions like envy 
and hatred in one's heart,

1349
00:12:15,497 --> 00:12:17,407
and makes one act on them.

1350
00:12:17,697 --> 00:12:19,637
Envy and hatred...

1351
00:12:19,817 --> 00:12:24,427
And since you don't possess such 
emotions, it wouldn't affect you.

1352
00:12:24,427 --> 00:12:28,007
That's why someone used it 
to manipulate those girls' hearts.

1353
00:12:28,347 --> 00:12:31,857
In other words, you might be their target.

1354
00:12:31,857 --> 00:12:34,107
Me?! Why?!

1355
00:12:34,327 --> 00:12:35,627
I don't know.

1356
00:12:35,627 --> 00:12:38,027
We have no way of knowing 
who it was, either.

1357
00:12:38,027 --> 00:12:40,737
At any rate, please be 
as careful as possible.

1358
00:12:41,087 --> 00:12:44,687
Be sure you don't try to do
anything on your own.

1359
00:12:45,127 --> 00:12:46,377
All right...

1360
00:12:49,187 --> 00:12:52,237
<i>Wait... If I'm their target...</i>

1361
00:12:52,667 --> 00:12:55,527
Then why did Maria disappear?

1362
00:12:55,527 --> 00:12:57,307
She has nothing to do with this!

1363
00:12:57,537 --> 00:13:01,167
Yes, but she has light magic.

1364
00:13:01,167 --> 00:13:04,197
Dark magic normally can't be detected,

1365
00:13:04,197 --> 00:13:07,787
but it's said that those with light magic 
are the only ones who can.

1366
00:13:08,187 --> 00:13:09,607
You mean...

1367
00:13:10,017 --> 00:13:13,297
Maria-san sensed something after that incident

1368
00:13:13,297 --> 00:13:15,237
and made contact with the perpetrator,

1369
00:13:15,237 --> 00:13:16,817
who then abducted her.

1370
00:13:17,177 --> 00:13:18,907
That is my deduction.

1371
00:13:20,687 --> 00:13:22,367
It can't be...

1372
00:13:23,647 --> 00:13:28,387
I can't believe people could 
be born with dark magic.

1373
00:13:28,387 --> 00:13:32,537
No, dark magic isn't something 
that anyone is born with.

1374
00:13:32,537 --> 00:13:35,177
It has to be acquired.

1375
00:13:35,177 --> 00:13:37,977
Acquired? How?

1376
00:13:38,477 --> 00:13:41,037
It requires a particular ritual.

1377
00:13:41,037 --> 00:13:42,177
A ritual?

1378
00:13:42,397 --> 00:13:47,647
It can be acquired by offering 
a human life in a ritual.

1379
00:13:47,807 --> 00:13:49,247
In other words...

1380
00:13:49,247 --> 00:13:52,937
it's acquired in exchange 
for someone else's life.

1381
00:13:58,757 --> 00:13:59,957
What is this place?

1382
00:14:14,977 --> 00:14:16,967
What happened to all of you?!

1383
00:14:16,967 --> 00:14:19,797
Wake up! Please, wake up!

1384
00:14:20,047 --> 00:14:22,507
<i>Why... How...</i>

1385
00:14:23,177 --> 00:14:25,557
<i>If this was the ending 
that was waiting for me,</i>

1386
00:14:26,087 --> 00:14:29,767
<i>it would've been far better 
for me to be doomed alone!</i>

1387
00:14:30,227 --> 00:14:32,477
<i>Why?!</i>

1388
00:14:35,947 --> 00:14:37,257
A dream...

1389
00:14:37,857 --> 00:14:41,407
Because we were talking 
about dark magic before I went to sleep?

1390
00:14:43,737 --> 00:14:47,897
<i>It's acquired in exchange 
for someone else's life.</i>

1391
00:14:50,887 --> 00:14:52,847
<i>That future can't be real.</i>

1392
00:14:53,497 --> 00:14:54,977
<i>In the world of the game,</i>

1393
00:14:54,977 --> 00:14:59,717
<i>the only one whose life was ever in danger 
was the villainess, Catarina Claes.</i>

